Z||000000||3.8T Fiero GT||11-20-2001||08:35 PM||||Finally got to take the primered '87 GT for a good boot 2day around the neighbourhood (NO exhaust, hehe!) as it is going for paint 2morrow!  THEN comes the hibernation where its new heart transplant comes  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">  not to mention other goodies!<P>I just wanted to say it was SO fun drivin it again, I have limited time behind the wheel of my Fiero since i just bought it!<P>So do all of u remember your first drives???<P>------------------<BR>*Your ASS here*   <IMG SRC="http://www.plaudersmilies.de/rough/zzwhip.gif"> <BR><B>"A 3.8T makes and excellent "RICE" cooker"</B>||||reg||10
Z||000001||4UMLA1||11-20-2001||09:02 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by 3.8T Fiero GT:<BR><B> So do all of u remember your first drives???<P></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><BR>Yea, it was about 3.5 years ago when I got my 88 GT.  I couldn't get out of the car <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">  I just drove and drove it for days.  I still find myself just getting in the car and just driving around, great fun they are to drive, and you know what the best thing is?  I love going past people and seeing them look at the car, it sends goose bumps up and down my spin each time it happens.  I like to talk to people about my car also.  It seams like each time I go out, at least 1 person will ask about the car, I love it <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><BR>Is there any way you could give me a ball park figure of how much it cost you to have the 3.8 put into your car? <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>||||reg||10
Z||000002||FieroHarry||11-20-2001||09:45 PM||||My first drive was almost 4 years ago.<BR>Man was it scary, had to replace the entire suspension and steering components.<P>4Th drive was the memorable one!<BR>Each and every time I drive my car I take a different route. Just to make it last a little longer than needed.<BR>I love the looks you get from kids though, they see a little "Hot Wheels" car and just smile, point and say "Mom, Dad, look at it"<P>Then they grow up and drive rice cars later in life so we can smoke-em   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>------------------<P><B>"If you want to blend in, take the bus!"</B><P>[This message has been edited by FieroHarry (edited 11-20-2001).]<p>[This message has been edited by FieroHarry (edited 11-20-2001).]||||reg||14
Z||000003||3.8T Fiero GT||11-22-2001||11:26 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by 4UMLA1:<BR><B> [QUOTE]Originally posted by 3.8T Fiero GT:<BR>[b] So do all of u remember your first drives???<P></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><BR>Is there any way you could give me a ball park figure of how much it cost you to have the 3.8 put into your car?  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><BR>[/B][/QUOTE]<P>well yeah, in general the swap would be about $2500 CDN dollars for the 3.8 SC motor, as for labour well that depends who does it or where u go, probably around $1000-$1500 CDN dollars.  (u convert it to US  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">)<P>as for myself, my situation is different cause myself and best buddy (a mechanic) are doing the swap so labour is almost free, but i am giving him $500 to help me with it.  the motor only cost me $800  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"> cause i bought it with NO supercharger since i am doing turbo, i bought the motor from my buddy who has another for his cavalier with a good SC.  i got the motor cheaper cause got it from a buddy.<P>so it isnt too bad, especially considering how much power u get and compared to swaps for imports.....the BEST swap for the dollar,  im sure most would agree with me.<P>i luv the fact that i SHOULD have a sub 13 sec. car for well under $10,000 CDN ($6500+ USD)with paint, rims, motor, suspension, brakes, etc.<P>enjoy...<P>------------------<BR>*Your ASS here*   <IMG SRC="http://www.plaudersmilies.de/rough/zzwhip.gif"> <BR><B>"A 3.8T makes and excellent "RICE" cooker"</B>||||reg||1
Z||000004||LoW_KeY||11-23-2001||05:36 AM||||OOh man do I ever! hehe..<P>well actually my 2nd fiero was the one to remember.<P>I couldn't drive stick to well so I was like hey why not get some practice I drove it 167 miles around my city just practicing and having fun! hehe <P>I still get that same urge once I pull it from the garage after winter its like ooooh yeah! and I get the stares from everyone.. then "your car sucks!" but why do they stare? jealous people you gotta love'em  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>------------------<BR>    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/kc.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000005||Master_Sushi||11-23-2001||09:58 AM||||My fiero drive in a fiero was an 86GT I test drove. I beleave the engine was moded out a bit so it was quite fast. I didn't really get on it though because I was with the owner  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif">. It was an auto also,  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smiley_zz.gif"> so not much fun.<BR>I got my 88 coupe about 2 years ago now, this thing I had allot of fun with. First time I drove it the tires all had about 8lbs of PSI. So it wasnt that fun, and almost scarey on the highway. Stupid owned didnt take care of the car!<BR>I'm on an 84se I drive daily. This is the 4.10 4 speed and its a BLAST to drive. I have done a few little performance mods also. Its by far the most fun fiero I've ever driven. The first time I drove it?.... Well I would rather not remember that, the car almost cought on fire, and parts were falling off as I test drove it around the block..  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">||||reg||1
